<title>FINLAND: RAUTE WINS FIM 50 MLN VENEER LINE ORDER.</title>
<headline>RAUTE WINS FIM 50 MLN VENEER LINE ORDER.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish engineering group Raute said on Tuesday its Raute Wood unit had won a veneer production line order worth 50 million markka from Metsaliitto's Finnforest's unit.</p>
<p>&quot;Delivery is scheduled for spring 1998,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>&quot;After the expansion, Finnforest's Suolahti veneer plant will be Europe's largest with a capacity of about 250,000 cubic metres a year,&quot; Raute said.  </p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 248, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
